thML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65a"}, {"id": "d2aae0", "text": "(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> III, (B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> I, (C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> II, (D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9942"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the following circuit, the correct relation between output <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>Y</mi></mfenced></math> and inputs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> will be</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9d2a5440-9828-4d56-a04e-9f177f90229c-1.jpg?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 185px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a351d7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65d"}, {"id": "822d33", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65e"}, {"id": "d8fdda", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></menclose></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d65f"}, {"id": "523299", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></menclose></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d660"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d661", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["6162fb636ed13040ec84e521"], "question": {"text": "<p>The resistivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of semiconductor varies with temperature. Which of the following curve represents the correct behaviour?</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "894871", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc3117041-c1ca-4a9f-a96c-3eef345a9e75-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 125px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d662"}, {"id": "60bf25", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F08547b14-823b-4c0c-88e6-3df9910d0d36-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d663"}, {"id": "427bc6", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F64d6638a-fbed-470b-a581-e0a8e20e2a7d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d664"}, {"id": "c27d23", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F61ddf3ed-068c-4108-883d-45eaa56914a3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d665"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d666", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb7"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following gives a reversible operation?"}, "options": [{"id": "693399", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff6427356-2c90-424a-831b-671586c0f22a.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d667"}, {"id": "32b2ae", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1481c81f-b663-42ef-8aea-36ee6141755e.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d668"}, {"id": "792407", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7cafe35b-1e84-4ab6-92b6-f9d18fe89204.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d669"}, {"id": "94a149", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5b46cc1a-13a1-4715-9d18-76f703f65002.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b5e6478ae845c43c5ed6"], "concepts": ["61ea9c853b8d9d376421821d"], "question": {"text": "The acceptor level of a p-type semiconductor is $6 \\mathrm{eV}$. The maximum wavelength of light which can create a hole would be : Given $\\mathrm{hc}=1242 \\mathrm{eV} \\mathrm{nm}$."}, "options": [{"id": "ba5765", "text": "$414 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66c"}, {"id": "44a8a6", "text": "$103.5 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66d"}, {"id": "2c8954", "text": "$207 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66e"}, {"id": "95f22a", "text": "$407 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d66f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d670", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5647"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following statements:\nA. The junction area of solar cell is made very narrow compared to a photo diode.\nB. Solar cells are not connected with any external bias.\nC. LED is made of lightly doped p-n junction.\nD. Increase of forward current results in continuous increase of LED light intensity.\nE. LEDs have to be connected in forward bias for emission of light.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "181875", "text": "B, E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d671"}, {"id": "e5bb49", "text": "B, D, E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d672"}, {"id": "3f6a9c", "text": "A, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d673"}, {"id": "c2ed01", "text": "A, C, E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d674"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d675", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["6117b64c478ae845c43c6816"], "question": {"text": "<p><strong>Statement I:</strong> By doping silicon semiconductors with pentavalent&nbsp;material, the electrons&nbsp;density increases.</p><p><strong>Statement II:</strong> The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo></math>type&nbsp;of semiconductor has a net negative charge.</p><p>In&nbsp;the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "71b652", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d676"}, {"id": "6194e4", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d677"}, {"id": "1e0a13", "text": "Statement I&nbsp;is false but Statement II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d678"}, {"id": "3d7f3d", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d679"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470c"], "question": {"text": "Which of the diode circuit shows correct biasing used for the measurement of dynamic resistance of p-n junction diode :"}, "options": [{"id": "7dee3e", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F-y2ZguBDcpN3-WLAiuNZyZMYYO3ya8CQ4I0t65scmSE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67b"}, {"id": "8d5c12", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb86B4UBPR4I5Pu1ZHloz35XrZUCoxM2gWN_hFCkbLI8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67c"}, {"id": "26609d", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FqlFGog0jcuY4OghkphKfJuZu7cRWgebn7U8_bBxKXEg.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67d"}, {"id": "1b11f2", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd6I8a8kKdG-44W8wvxOxbGsvc5rpLeG1-LVZN9dy7YE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d67f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacd5"], "question": {"text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> characteristics of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction diode in forward bias is shown in the figure. The ratio of dynamic resistance, corresponding to forward bias voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respective is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F41e3a4ad-f94b-4662-a6a4-de8085e81d64-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 166px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "804994", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d680"}, {"id": "e65a3e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d681"}, {"id": "0bfa20", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>40</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d682"}, {"id": "2ff519", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d683"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d684", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea2fb"], "question": {"text": "For extrinsic semiconductors; when doping level is increased;"}, "options": [{"id": "13887a", "text": "Fermi-level of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>- type semiconductors will not be affected.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d685"}, {"id": "2db85b", "text": "Fermi-level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>-type semiconductor will go upward and Fermi-level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>-type semiconductors will go downward.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d686"}, {"id": "c788ea", "text": "Fermi-level of both p-type and n-type semiconductors will go upward for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and downward for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></math> is Fermi temperature.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d687"}, {"id": "218f79", "text": "Fermi-level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>- type semiconductors will go downward and Fermi-level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>- type semiconductor will go upward.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d688"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d689", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["6176f3e76581241c7072a005"], "question": {"text": "Identify the solar cell characteristics from the following options :"}, "options": [{"id": "6a486c", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapi