/mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d692"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:46.635Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:46.635Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6d9"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6d7", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6bb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b5e6478ae845c43c5ed6"], "concepts": ["61ea9c853b8d9d376421821d"], "question": {"text": "The energy band gap of semiconducting material to produce violet (wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#8491;</mo></math>) LED is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>eV</mi></math>. (Round off to the nearest integer)."}, "options": [{"id": "016441", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6bc"}, {"id": "9866e2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6bd"}, {"id": "5f1a36", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6be"}, {"id": "68ab01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6bf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea2fb"], "question": {"text": "In a semiconductor, the number density of intrinsic charge carriers at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the semiconductor is doped with an impurity atom, the hole density increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>22</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The electron density in the doped semiconductor is _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "dd0778", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c1"}, {"id": "fa0087", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c2"}, {"id": "8ec890", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c3"}, {"id": "471c6d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "A potential divider circuit is connected with a dc source of $20 \\mathrm{~V}$, a light emitting diode of glow in voltage $1.8 \\mathrm{~V}$ and a zener diode of breakdown voltage of $3.2 \\mathrm{~V}$. The length (PR) of the resistive wire is $20 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The minimum length of PQ to just glow the LED is _____$\\mathrm{cm}$\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FGs54MkZHGs-Hmq-BGuX7Sa_pekl5WoGjbt1SfdsTIGk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "d91ac0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c6"}, {"id": "bb6230", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c7"}, {"id": "f80b94", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c8"}, {"id": "4cbb62", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6c9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6ca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa392"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the logic circuit shown in the figure, if input <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> respectively, the output at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> would be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _________.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F46e9c281-3b90-4d58-8f65-38a9f4e7304c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 369px; height: 116px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a1e909", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6cb"}, {"id": "a83231", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6cc"}, {"id": "3c569b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6cd"}, {"id": "6ed26c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6ce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d6cf", "type": "n